<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $41.7 mln Sept 10.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $41.7 mln Sept 10.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $41.7 million deficit on September 10 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON SEPTEMBER 10</p>
<p>Exports: $227.5 million</p>
<p>Imports: $125.9 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $103.7 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $247 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $41.7 million</p>
<p>SEPTEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.489 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $965 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $858 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.397 billion</p>
<p>Net deficit: $15 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
